        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "When rescuers searched through the remains of a collapsed apartment building after the earthquake, they expected to find silence. Instead, somewhere deep beneath the broken concrete and twisted metal, they heard the faint sound of a dog barking. The bark was weak and exhausted, but it continued every few minutes, guiding workers toward one specific section of the rubble.\n\nFor hours, crews carefully dug through the unstable debris, unsure of what they would find underneath. As they got closer, they realized the dog had been trapped in a tiny pocket beneath the collapsed floor, barely able to move. But even after being buried for so long, the animal had never stopped barking.\n\nWhen rescuers finally reached the source of the sound, they found a heartbreaking scene. Curled tightly beneath the dog’s body was a small baby, shielded from falling debris and dust. The dog had positioned itself over the child the entire time, protecting the baby from the collapse while trapped underground. Weak and dehydrated, the child was still alive.\n\nBoth the baby and the dog were pulled from the rubble together as exhausted rescuers looked on in disbelief. Witnesses later said the dog could barely stand after the rescue, but still tried to stay close to the child it had protected for hours beneath the ruins. ❤️"
        },
